INTRODUCTION:	The purpose in this example is to show how to use the custom format. 	In this example, the line delimiter is custom and can be longer than one character.EXAMPLES:	In this examples, only two C-formatting functions are used: one for import, and one for export.	All variations of line delimiters can be done in the sql scripts based on these C-functions.		In the examples you'll find the following:		* line_delim.c - the C-formatting functions		* lineDelimIn.sql - the sql scripts for Readable External Tables (RET)		* lineDelimOut.sql - the sql scripts for Writable External Tables (WET)				* lineDelimIn.tbl - the data to be loaded		USAGE:	To run these examples do the following steps:		1. Run:		> make		2. Run gpfdist. <path> should point to the directory where "lineDelimOut.tbl" is in 		> gpfdist -d <path>		3.	Open the sql files, and in the LOCATION clause, change the host name from localhost to your host name		Run sql scripts:		> psql -f lineDelimIn.sql		> psql -f lineDelimOut.sql		NOTICE:	* This program was tested only on Red hat 5.5 and on OS X 10.7.3 .  	* Notice that one C formatting function can be useful for different line delimiters.